diagnostic is that of the base process; for a \link[=tsmod-class]{tsmod} model the data
(on the original scale) are first transformed by the margin.

With \code{B > 0} the diagnostic is repeated for \code{B} series simulated from the model
(the parameters are taken as given, so parameter uncertainty is ignored) and the
pointwise \code{level} interval of the simulated values is returned in \code{lo} and \code{hi}: if the
data's values fall inside, they are what the model typically produces.
